      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "external-iteration",
          "heading": "External Iteration",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Requires manually controlling the loop (either with Iterator or for-each).",
                "Developer manages both:  for (Employee emp : empList) {\n    System.out.println(emp.getCountry());\n}",
                "This is external iteration, as the control of iteration lies with the developer."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 34,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "internal-iteration-with-lambda-expressions",
          "heading": "Internal Iteration with Lambda Expressions",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Java 8 introduced internal iteration using lambda expressions.",
                "Focuses only on what needs to be done, abstracting away the iteration logic.",
                "Achieved using the forEach() method from the Iterable interface. empList.forEach(emp -> System.out.println(emp.getCountry()));",
                "Benefits: "
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 34,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "behind-the-scenes",
          "heading": "Behind the Scenes",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "forEach() is a default method added to the Iterable interface in Java 8.",
                "It accepts a Consumer functional interface: default void forEach(Consumer<? super T> action)",
                "Enables internal iteration by abstracting the control flow of looping."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 35,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "advantages-of-internal-iteration",
          "heading": "Advantages of Internal Iteration",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Encourages functional programming style.",
                "Allows for parallel processing when used with streams (to be covered later).",
                "Promotes cleaner code with lambda expressions and method references."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 25,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    }
